WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.296 --> 00:00:05.437
Kathleen and Mabel were still at their tea party.

2
00:00:05.477 --> 00:00:07.518
Suddenly they both felt the same way.

3
00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:11.481
They must go to the Temple of Flora!

4
00:00:11.521 --> 00:00:17.444
They didn't know why, but they knew they must go.

5
00:00:31.976 --> 00:00:36.359
When Gerald and Jimmy yelled for help, Kathleen and Mabel were ready to help.

6
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.142
The girls opened the door, and the boys were free.

7
00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:44.704
Kathleen hugged her brothers.

8
00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:50.387
They spoke about their adventures in London and in the secret passage.

9
00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:54.649
"Did you leave that Ugly-Wugly in London?"

10
00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:55.770
asked Mabel.

11
00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.592
"Yes," said Gerald.

12
00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:03.255
"Now we'll seal the ring in an envelope so no one else gets in trouble."

13
00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:08.860
"But I didn't have a chance to use it," protested Kathleen.

14
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.743
"You've seen what it does," said Gerald.

15
00:01:12.763 --> 00:01:15.225
"Why would you want to use it?"

16
00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:19.809
"I'd make it do nice things," said Kathleen.

17
00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:24.713
"Let's just put it back in the treasure room," said Mabel.

18
00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:27.716
"It was a bad idea to take it."

19
00:01:30.432 --> 00:01:32.033
They walked over to the castle.

20
00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.835
In the treasure room, Mabel pushed the secret button.

21
00:01:37.615 --> 00:01:38.695
The panels slid up.

22
00:01:41.356 --> 00:01:43.517
All the jewels sparkled on the shelves.

23
00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:46.619
Mabel took the ring from Gerald.

24
00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:52.241
"I don't even know what to call that ring," said Kathleen.

25
00:01:52.261 --> 00:01:54.682
"The wishing ring?

26
00:01:55.082 --> 00:01:56.523
The invisibility ring?"

27
00:01:56.543 --> 00:01:59.884
"Oh!" Mabel put the ring on.

28
00:02:01.324 --> 00:02:02.624
"I understand now.

29
00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:04.905
The ring is whatever you say it is.

30
00:02:05.405 --> 00:02:08.266
It made us invisible because I said that's what it does.

31
00:02:08.726 --> 00:02:11.227
Then it became a wishing ring during our play."

32
00:02:17.249 --> 00:02:19.569
still a wishing ring," said Jimmy.

33
00:02:19.589 --> 00:02:22.590
"No," said Mabel.

34
00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.611
"We've already had that.

35
00:02:25.051 --> 00:02:28.412
I say it's a ring that makes the wearer four meters high."

36
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.861
She was still wearing the ring.

37
00:02:32.822 --> 00:02:34.943
Even as she spoke, she started to grow.

38
00:02:36.344 --> 00:02:38.526
Soon she was four meters high.

39
00:02:40.047 --> 00:02:41.688
But she didn't grow much in width.

40
00:02:43.009 --> 00:02:45.070
So she was very, very skinny.

41
00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:50.494
"Oh, Mabel, that was silly," said Kathleen.

42
00:02:50.514 --> 00:02:54.096
"Who knows how long this spell will last?"

43
00:02:55.557 --> 00:02:57.819
"What am I going to do now?"

44
00:02:58.379 --> 00:02:59.140
moaned Mabel.

45
00:03:00.744 --> 00:03:04.765
"We must hide you until you're back to your right size," said Gerald.

46
00:03:04.785 --> 00:03:07.606
"How about in an empty room?"

47
00:03:07.626 --> 00:03:12.147
"I'd rather stay outside," said Mabel.

48
00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:16.568
"It's a good thing my aunt thinks I'm staying overnight with you."

49
00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:18.929
The children went outside.

50
00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:22.310
Mabel had to crawl to fit through doors.

51
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.051
Outside she crept behind some bushes so no one would see her.

52
00:03:28.071 --> 00:03:30.392
"Aren't you hungry?"

53
00:03:30.928 --> 00:03:31.568
asked Jimmy.

54
00:03:31.588 --> 00:03:35.030
"Oh yes," said Mabel.

55
00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:38.932
"I'll write to my aunt, and she'll send us a picnic."

56
00:03:40.812 --> 00:03:43.113
Mabel used Gerald's notebook to write a note.

57
00:03:45.995 --> 00:03:49.236
Dear Aunt, May we have some things for a picnic?

58
00:03:49.636 --> 00:03:50.637
Gerald will bring them.

59
00:03:51.017 --> 00:03:53.158
I'd come myself, but I'm tired.

60
00:03:53.498 --> 00:03:55.799
I think I've been growing rather fast.

61
00:03:56.219 --> 00:04:01.429
Your loving niece, Mabel Gerald went to fetch the food.

62
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:12.292
When he came back, they had a splendid picnic of bread, cake, gooseberries, and milk.

63
00:04:13.292 --> 00:04:15.673
Gerald noticed the dinosaur statue nearby.

64
00:04:15.693 --> 00:04:19.534
"He must have eaten some good meals in his time."

65
00:04:20.574 --> 00:04:21.574
Kathleen giggled.

66
00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.235
"We fed him today."

67
00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:26.716
"What do you mean?"

68
00:04:27.216 --> 00:04:27.816
asked Jimmy.

69
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:34.322
Kathleen explained how she and Mabel had hidden the Ugly-Wuglies' clothes in the dinosaur's belly.

70
00:04:34.342 --> 00:04:38.944
"We can take them home now," said Gerald.

71
00:04:38.964 --> 00:04:43.906
"I've got an idea," Kathleen suddenly said.

72
00:04:43.926 --> 00:04:45.887
"Give me the ring."

73
00:04:51.769 --> 00:04:53.150
She ran ahead of the others.

74
00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:57.772
"I say this is a wishing ring."

75
00:04:58.884 --> 00:05:01.645
She believed the ring would change if she renamed it.

76
00:05:02.986 --> 00:05:06.567
When they reached the dinosaur, Kathleen climbed up into its belly.

77
00:05:09.188 --> 00:05:13.050
She handed down the clothes and other Ugly-Wugly things to her brothers.

78
00:05:14.051 --> 00:05:15.591
"Wait a minute," said Gerald.

79
00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:17.012
"I'm coming up."

80
00:05:19.873 --> 00:05:21.214
"Isn't it nice in here?"

81
00:05:21.714 --> 00:05:22.554
said Kathleen.

82
00:05:22.574 --> 00:05:25.716
"I wish I were a statue.

83
00:05:25.736 --> 00:05:31.587
Oh!" And just like that, Kathleen turned into a statue.
